#### 🏛️ Phase 1: Realistic First-Phase Revenue (Years 1–2 / VCBIP Pilot Window)
During Phase 1, revenue depends **100% on fixed B2G enterprise contracts** with sovereign border control agencies, funded through existing trade corridor modernization budgets:

1. **`R.1` Setup & Custom Integration Fee (€15,000 – €30,000):** One-time fee for edge hardware schema configuration, API bridging to existing customs databases, and SCADA control room setup.
2. **`R.2` Annual B2G SaaS Platform License (€25,000 – €60,000 / year):** Fixed annual subscription covering the hosted sub-500ms decision engine, shadow sandbox server maintenance, and live SCADA digital twin software updates.
3. **`R.3` Remote Governance & System Maintenance Fee (€5,000 – €7,500 / year):** Recurring annual retainer for operational uptime SLAs, data anonymization maintenance, and system health monitoring.

#### 🚀 Phase 2: Future & Speculative Revenue Streams (Years 3+ / Commercial Scaling)
All volumetric, usage-based, and market-dependent revenue streams are explicitly deferred to Phase 2, unlocking only after live fleet onboarding and regulatory MRV accreditation:

* **`R.4` Fast-Lane Transaction Micro-Billing (€15.00 / cleared transit):** Volumetric fee billed per pre-authorized fast-lane clearance.
* **`R.5` Green-Credit Scope 3 ESG Audit Fee (€2.50 / compliance certificate):** Automated B2B compliance certificate fee generated for 3PL carriers and corporate shippers meeting EU CSDDD/CSRD reporting standards.
* **`R.6` Certified Carbon Credit Trading (€80.00 / Tonne $\text{CO}_2$):** Monetization of verified avoided diesel emissions on carbon credit spot markets.

